WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.853 --> 00:00:02.945
(suspenseful music)

00:00:02.945 --> 00:00:04.163
- [Presenter] The Loch Ness Monster

00:00:04.163 --> 00:00:07.439
is one of our most enduring myths.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:11.163
People have sought its
secrets for over 1,500 years

00:00:11.163 --> 00:00:14.033
but only one man has
devoted his entire life

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.866
to learning the truth.

00:00:17.023 --> 00:00:18.356
Alone, in a van.

00:00:19.736 --> 00:00:20.736
By the loch.

00:00:24.316 --> 00:00:28.253
And no, he's not a wacko,
it's just his thing.

00:00:28.253 --> 00:00:31.797
(playful instrumental music)

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.461
- My name's Steve Feltham,

00:00:33.461 --> 00:00:35.503
and for the last 25 years

00:00:35.503 --> 00:00:39.670
I've been a full-time hunter
of the Loch Ness Monster.

00:00:41.422 --> 00:00:44.675
I first came to Loch Ness when
I was a seven-year-old boy

00:00:44.675 --> 00:00:48.422
and found this set of
caravans with this gang

00:00:48.422 --> 00:00:52.023
of grown men hunting for
monsters in Loch Ness.

00:00:52.023 --> 00:00:54.241
And I thought, that's amazing.

00:00:54.241 --> 00:00:57.691
That would be the life for
me, I'd love to do that!

00:00:57.691 --> 00:00:58.997
- [Presenter] And so he did.

00:00:58.997 --> 00:01:02.127
Twenty five years ago he quit
his job, sold his house,

00:01:02.127 --> 00:01:05.029
bought this van, and pursued his passion.

00:01:05.029 --> 00:01:06.670
He now holds the Guinness Record

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:10.587
for the longest continuous
search at Loch Ness.

00:01:14.739 --> 00:01:18.080
- In all my time here I've only seen one

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.663
possible sighting of something.

00:01:22.084 --> 00:01:23.805
All you saw was a spray of water

00:01:23.805 --> 00:01:25.380
off of the back of something,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.214
boff, boff, boff, boff, boff,

00:01:27.214 --> 00:01:29.655
like a torpedo shooting through.

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:32.459
To this day that remains a mystery to me

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:34.126
as to what that was.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.396
That was in the first year of being here

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:39.970
and I thought, right, this
job's gonna be really easy.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:41.506
That's one sighting.

00:01:41.506 --> 00:01:44.069
25 years later I'm still sat here waiting

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:46.152
for that second sighting.

00:01:47.463 --> 00:01:49.815
Some people think it's giant eels,

00:01:49.815 --> 00:01:53.261
some people think there's a rip in time.

00:01:53.261 --> 00:01:54.690
Others believe there's a spaceship

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.680
on the bottom of the loch.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.198
It's more likely to turn
out to be big catfish

00:02:00.198 --> 00:02:03.781
than a spaceship on
the bottom of the loch.

00:02:07.737 --> 00:02:11.068
The reason I sit here and I
try and solve this mystery

00:02:11.068 --> 00:02:14.296
is because that's what
makes my heart sing.

00:02:14.296 --> 00:02:17.898
People say, "Is it lifestyle
or is it the mystery?"

00:02:17.898 --> 00:02:19.182
It's both.

00:02:19.182 --> 00:02:23.717
My life contains freedom,
adventure, unpredictability,

00:02:23.717 --> 00:02:26.551
and the chance of one of the
world's greatest discoveries,

00:02:26.551 --> 00:02:29.551
should I ever happen to find Nessie.

00:02:30.498 --> 00:02:31.680
It's a dream come true.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.255
If that little
seven-year-old boy could see

00:02:33.255 --> 00:02:37.338
what became of him, he
wouldn't believe his luck.

